  "curation_criteria": "The 28 CURATED_PAIRS were selected DETERMINISTICALLY by gap-spanning over the committed 1.7B fine-tune ladder (`readout_invariance.select_curated_pairs`: near-ties oversampled + mid + large-gap anchors), NOT hand-picked for clean 1.7B behavior. The 5 language pairs span |\u0394_pr|. The 18 congruence pairs are the fixed prior-association roster (minus 3 buildability DROP_PAIRS). All claims are CONDITIONAL on this Qwen3-1.7B-derived pair set (we test whether the 1.7B ranking survives, not an unbiased universal hierarchy).",
  "config": {
    "dtype": "bfloat16 forward / fp32 probe fit (activations cast to float32; NOT standardized \u2014 matches the committed instrument; claim is phrased as 'probe-derived ranking')",
    "limit_per_cell": 200,
    "seeds": [
      0,
      1,
      2
    ],
    "wrap": "none",
    "representation": "last (raw-text last non-pad token; add_special_tokens=False -> no BOS/EOS, no chat template; identical construction across tokenizers)",
    "probe": "sklearn LogisticRegression(C=1.0, max_iter=1000), 75/25 stratified split per seed",
    "delta_definition": "oriented held-out log-odds toward f1, seed-mean, at the final hidden state (primary); robustness rules: deep-band median + argmin-CE",
    "gap_strata": {
      "large_well_separated": ">= 5.0",
      "near_tie": "< 1.5",
      "note": "probe-scale thresholds (probe |\u0394_pr| ~half the fine-tune scale), calibrated to the 1.7B reference distribution"
    }
  },
  "layer_rule": {
    "primary": "the FINAL hidden state (post-final-norm) \u2014 a FIXED, unambiguous, architecture-agnostic read position; where the committed 1.7B probe ladder lives (layer 28 of 28). NOT the argmin-CE layer (degenerate). \u0394_pr = seed-mean held-out log-odds at the final layer.",
    "robustness": "ALSO report every headline metric at (a) the deep-band [0.75, 1.0] MEDIAN and (b) the argmin-mean-held-in-CE layer (the committed rule; degenerate here, chosen over NON-language pairs only). The read's SIGN is stable across the deep band, so the ranking/winner conclusions should not depend on the rule.",
    "why_not_argmin": "hidden >> texts/cell -> diagonal trivially separable -> held-in CE saturates (~0) across ~50 deep layers -> argmin tie-break is float noise (design review)."
  },
