  "segment_predictions": [
    "P1 (HEADLINE, confirmatory): Spearman(NON-language per-feature s_pr vs 1.7B, deep-band rule) >= 0.7 => ranking PRESERVED for that model; near 0 => a clean non-transfer. Expect preservation across the Qwen scale axis + Llama; OLMo (different corpus) is the most likely to break \u2014 if any model's Spearman is near 0 it should be OLMo.",
    "P2 (confirmatory): the 16 should-never-flip anchors (large probe gap, non-fragile) keep their 1.7B winner in EVERY model. STRICT bar: 100%; PRACTICAL bar: a flip count consistent with read-noise (>= n-1 of n, or a binomial test vs the coin-flip baseline), since some anchors have thin held-out cells (flagged per-pair).",
    "P3 (confirmatory): near-ties are where flips are ALLOWED \u2014 winner-agreement on the 'near' stratum should sit near the tie/majority baseline; flips there are uninformative.",
    "P4 (EXPLORATORY \u2014 raw |\u0394_pr| is NOT comparable across models/dims, so this is NOT confirmatory): within the post-trained Qwen axis, does a SCALE-FREE decisiveness \u2014 the fraction of pairs whose |\u0394_pr| exceeds 2x its own seed SD (signal-to-noise), and the hard-accuracy>=0.9 fraction \u2014 rise with scale? Computed at the fixed deep-band rule; raw-nat magnitude is reported only descriptively.",
    "P5 (descriptive): the prior-association winners on the 18 congruence pairs are mostly preserved on well-separated pairs; any flips concentrate in the entangled/near-tie congruence pairs and may differ for OLMo vs the Qwen/Llama family.",
    "P6 (confirmatory): the base controls (Qwen3-1.7B-Base, Qwen3-8B-Base) rank-agree with their post-trained twins at Spearman >= 0.8, so post-training is a SMALL move vs cross-family/corpus differences \u2014 licensing the mixed base/post family comparison. Family/corpus conclusions are interpreted only AFTER checking P6.",
    "P7 (EXPLORATORY): language is layer-fragile (its probe \u0394_pr flips sign across layers \u2014 likely because non-English tokens route differently through the residual stream); it is EXCLUDED from every confirmatory pass/fail. Reported separately, with the with/without-language s_pr gap noted."
  ],
  "axis_level_criteria": {
    "scale_transfer": "passes iff qwen3_8b AND qwen3_32b pass P1+P2",
    "family_transfer": "passes iff llama31_8b passes P1+P2 (interpreted after P6)",
    "corpus_transfer": "passes iff olmo2_7b passes P1+P2 (interpreted after P6)",
    "post_training_invariance": "passes iff both base/post Qwen pairs pass P6"
  },
  "metrics": [
    "PRIMARY: Spearman + Kendall of NON-language s_pr vs 1.7B, with a PAIR-REFIT bootstrap CI (resample roster pairs, refit s_pr \u2014 pairs are coupled through the graph, so a feature-i.i.d. bootstrap understates correlation and is reported only descriptively). Also report with-language.",
    "Pairwise winner-agreement: fraction of curated pairs whose sign(\u0394_pr) matches the 1.7B, bootstrap CI, stratified by the 1.7B probe gap (large/mid/near), vs the near-tie/majority baseline.",
    "Per-target-model ADDITIVE-LAW diagnostics: in-sample R\u00b2, residual SD, leave-one-pair-out R\u00b2 (if the law collapses in a model, its s_pr ranking is ill-defined \u2014 itself a first-class finding).",
    "Layer-robustness: every headline metric re-reported at the final layer + argmin-CE layer.",
    "Diagonal-separability gate: per model, held-in val accuracy at the read layers must be >= 0.95 (expected to pass trivially given trivial separability; the gate's real value is catching a load/extract failure, NOT a representational one \u2014 stated so it isn't oversold).",
    "Scale-free decisiveness (P4, exploratory): fraction of pairs with |\u0394_pr|/seed-SD > 2, and hard-accuracy>=0.9 fraction, per model.",
    "C-sensitivity robustness (reference): confirm the headline signs/ranks are stable for C in {0.1, 1, 10} on the 1.7B (the probe is overparameterized; closes the regularization attack).",
    "Per-pair held-out N surfaced in data inspection (thin-cell anchors flagged)."
  ],
  "pass_bar": "'Ranking preserved' for a model <=> Spearman(NON-language s_pr vs 1.7B) >= 0.7 AND large-stratum winner-agreement meets the PRACTICAL bar (>= n-1 of the non-language anchors, or binomial p<0.01 vs coin-flip). The STRICT bar (100% anchor agreement) is reported alongside. Axis-level conclusions per `axis_level_criteria`. Negative/boundary results are FIRST-CLASS: a clean OLMo non-transfer is as real a finding as preservation.",
